 ## Session isolation and gateway contract
 
-Before reading bytes, `vision_inspect` resolves every requested id from uploaded image blocks in the calling agent's own session event stream. An unknown or cross-session id rejects the complete batch before any attachment read or gateway request. Duplicate ids and over-limit batches also fail before dispatch.
+`vision_inspect` accepts current-session `attachmentIds`, local image `paths`, or both. Before reading bytes, it resolves every requested id from uploaded image blocks or prior `vision/image-import` records in the calling agent's own session event stream. An unknown or cross-session id rejects the complete batch before any attachment or filesystem read and before any gateway request.
+
+Local paths resolve relative to the session workspace through the mounted `ctx.fs` backend; absolute paths use the same backend rules. The bridge accepts PNG/JPEG/WebP/GIF regular files, admits the complete path batch through the native attachment service, and appends only the resulting normalized references as one log-only `vision/image-import` event. It never stores source paths or image bytes in the session log. The combined references are content-id deduplicated and bounded by `maxImagesPerCall`, so later calls in this session may use the returned attachment ids without rereading the source files.
 
 The gateway receives one OpenAI-compatible chat-completions request containing the main model's complete delegated prompt plus data URLs for the authorized images. Model-visible results contain only `attachmentIds`, `summary`, `observations` (`text`, optional `region`, optional `confidence`), and `limitations`; endpoint, credential, remote model, timing, and internal error bodies are excluded.
 
@@ -70,11 +72,16 @@ Append-only: the new user message and notice extend the reusable request prefix.
 
 #### What the model sees
 
-The model sees the `vision_inspect` tool with `attachmentIds` and a complete delegated `prompt`; its description says to reuse recent tool results unless a new visual question, region, comparison, or missing observation requires another call.
+The model sees the `vision_inspect` tool with optional `attachmentIds`, optional `paths`, and a required complete delegated `prompt`. At least one image source is required. The concise descriptions are:
+
+- Tool: `Inspect conversation attachments or local image files with the configured vision model.`
+- `attachmentIds`: `Current-conversation attachment IDs to inspect.`
+- `paths`: `Image file paths to import into this conversation and inspect.`
+- `prompt`: `The complete visual question or inspection task.`
 
 #### Token effect
 
-The stable tool definition is present whenever the plugin is loaded. Each successful call adds one structured textual tool result; image bytes and data URLs exist only in the separate vision-gateway request.
+The stable tool definition is present whenever the plugin is loaded. A path call additionally adds one model-invisible import record containing normalized attachment references. Each successful call adds one structured textual tool result; source paths, image bytes, and data URLs never enter model history and the latter exist only in the separate vision-gateway request.
 
 #### KV Cache effect
 
